.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_STREAM_READ 3 2026-09-24 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_stream_read \- read decoded logical MPQ member bytes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_stream_read(mpq_file_stream_s *" stream ", uint8_t *" buffer ", libmpq__off_t " size ", libmpq__off_t *" transferred ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read up to \fIsize\fP decoded logical bytes, crossing sectors as needed. The
position advances only by successfully returned bytes. EOF and zero-length
reads succeed with zero transferred bytes. An error after earlier sectors
returns their count; bytes from a failing sector are not transferred.
.PP
Usable sector Adler-32 values are checked as sectors load. Arbitrary file
stream reads do not implicitly verify whole-file CRC32/MD5 attributes; use
.BR libmpq__file_verify (3)
for explicit whole-file integrity verification.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP for normal, short EOF, and zero-length reads.
.SH ERRORS
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP reports an invalid stream or nonzero read with a NULL
buffer. \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP reports an invalid size.
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_READ\fP reports a sector-checksum mismatch. Backing-I/O,
decryption, decompression, allocation, and malformed-data errors can also
propagate from the sector decoder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__file_stream_open (3),
.BR libmpq__file_verify (3)
